# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# fastembed-downloaded ONNX model cache (legacy backend artifacts)
.fastembed_cache/

# Signed Firefox extension artifacts. Committed so multi-machine deploys
# (laptop + desk + servers) can install without each one needing to re-sign
# against AMO - AMO publishes one .xpi per version and rejects re-uploads
# at the same version with `Version X.Y.Z already exists`. The publishing
# machine signs once, commits the .xpi, and every other machine that
# `git pull`s reuses it via sign::run's idempotency check. The
# .amo-upload-uuid sidecar stays tracked alongside so signing continues
# to target the same AMO listing.

# Generated extension manifest + schema. Produced fresh at sign/stage
# time from sb's CARGO_PKG_VERSION and the loaded config; the runtime
# materialises them into a tempfile::TempDir for web-ext sign. Inspect
# the current shape via `sb borg extension show`. These lines guard
# against accidental re-commit if a future regen verb writes here.
borg/clients/extension/manifest.json
borg/clients/extension/ingest-schema.json

# Claude Code runtime files
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
